Install the builtin mathjax distribution together with JSROOT

With builtin_mathjax=ON, the mathjax distribution is only unpacked into
js/mathjax in the build tree, but nothing installs it: the install rule for
JSROOT copies the js directory of the source tree. JSROOT loads
mathjax/es5/tex-svg.js relative to its own location (see
js/modules/base/latex.mjs), so an installed ROOT always falls back to the
CDN, and the builtin_mathjax option has no effect for the installation.

Install the distribution next to JSROOT, like in the build tree.

---
diff --git a/builtins/mathjax/CMakeLists.txt b/builtins/mathjax/CMakeLists.txt
index 7f25bc56ba1..773a66cc33b 100644
--- a/builtins/mathjax/CMakeLists.txt
+++ b/builtins/mathjax/CMakeLists.txt
@@ -8,3 +8,5 @@ ExternalProject_Add(
    SOURCE_DIR ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/js/mathjax/
    TIMEOUT 600
 )
+
+install(DIRECTORY ${CMAKE_BINARY_DIR}/js/mathjax/ DESTINATION ${CMAKE_INSTALL_JSROOTDIR}/mathjax ${DIR_PERMISSIONS})
